.SH "1\&.0\&.0"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
massive update - separated functions into separate modules
.IP "\(bu" 2
functions do not accept multiple types anymore - use different versions in their respective modules in some cases (eg\&. \fRObj\&.map\fP), or use \fRchars\fP or \fRvalues\fP in other cases to transform into a list
.IP "\(bu" 2
objects are no longer transformed into functions, simply use \fR(obj\&.)\fP in LiveScript to do that
.IP "\(bu" 2
browser version now using browserify - use \fRprelude = require('prelude-ls')\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
added \fRcompact\fP, \fRsplit\fP, \fRflatten\fP, \fRdifference\fP, \fRintersection\fP, \fRunion\fP, \fRcount-by\fP, \fRgroup-by\fP, \fRchars\fP, \fRunchars\fP, \fRapply\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
added \fRlists-to-obj\fP which takes a list of keys and list of values and zips them up into an object, and the converse \fRobj-to-lists\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
added \fRpairs-to-obj\fP which takes a list of pairs (2 element lists) and creates an object, and the converse \fRobj-to-pairs\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
removed \fRcons\fP, \fRappend\fP - use the concat operator
.IP "\(bu" 2
removed \fRcompose\fP - use the compose operator
.IP "\(bu" 2
removed \fRobj-to-func\fP - use partially applied access (eg\&. \fR(obj\&.)\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
removed \fRlength\fP - use \fR(\&.length)\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsort-by\fP renamed to \fRsort-with\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
added new \fRsort-by\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
removed \fRcompare\fP - just use the new \fRsort-by\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRbreak-it\fP renamed \fRbreak-list\fP, (\fRStr\&.break-str\fP for the string version)
.IP "\(bu" 2
added \fRStr\&.repeat\fP which creates a new string by repeating the input n times
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRunfold\fP as alias to \fRunfoldr\fP is no longer used
.IP "\(bu" 2
fixed up style and compiled with LiveScript 1\&.1\&.1
.IP "\(bu" 2
use Make instead of Slake
.IP "\(bu" 2
greatly improved tests
.PP
.SH "0\&.6\&.0"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
fixed various bugs
.IP "\(bu" 2
added \fRfix\fP, a fixpoint (Y combinator) for anonymous recursive functions
.IP "\(bu" 2
added \fRunfoldr\fP (alias \fRunfold\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
calling \fRreplicate\fP with a string now returns a list of strings
.IP "\(bu" 2
removed \fRpartial\fP, just use native partial application in LiveScript using the \fR_\fP placeholder, or currying
.IP "\(bu" 2
added \fRsort\fP, \fRsortBy\fP, and \fRcompare\fP
.PP
